# versions.env — the ONE home for every tool version of base and cloud.
#
# One line per pin, shell-sourceable `NAME=value`, exact versions, no ranges.
# The build generates `--build-arg NAME=value` for every line of this file
# (`versions_env_build_args` in _ctl/lib.sh; the base and cloud CI jobs generate
# the same list), and base/Dockerfile and cloud/Dockerfile declare each name as
# a value-less ARG at the top. Neither Dockerfile carries a hand-written pin: to
# change a version you edit 1 line HERE and nothing else. A missing pin FAILS
# the build at the pin gate and names the variable.
#
# There was a second mechanism until this file became the only one: base/
# Dockerfile carried its own `ARG NAME=value` block, 54 of its 55 pins were
# spelled in both places, and _ctl/tests/pin-mirroring.test.sh existed to hold
# the 2 copies to 1 value. A rule enforced by a test is a rule that can drift
# between merges; 1 home cannot.
#
# mobile/ and embedded/ still declare their own pins inline. They consume no
# build arg from this file, and closing THAT half is ledger #102. It was 3 files
# and is 2: zephyr/ and zephyr-devbox/ merged into embedded/, which moved no pin
# VALUE and no pin home to this file — it removed a home by making 2 images 1.
# The other half of #102 is closed: .ci/smoke.sh reads each of those 2 files as a
# second pin home with a class table of its own, so a pin of theirs is compared
# against the image or says in writing why it is not.
#
# The harness pins (claude/omp/codex) mirror eden harnesses/versions.env
# (ADR-0021). Until the consumer migration lands, the 2 files MUST move
# together, and that debt is recorded in gophersys/infrastructure
# docs/debt-register.md. runner/Dockerfile carried the same debt as a second
# home of CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION until D2 deleted it, so this file is the only home
# on this side of the mirror now.

# -------- base OS --------
# The ubuntu:24.04 INDEX digest, not a per-platform one: buildx still has to
# choose the manifest for the platform it builds. Under the moving tag, 2 builds
# of 1 commit produce 2 different operating systems. This row is the ONLY home
# of the digest — base/Dockerfile and cloud/Dockerfile each declare a value-less
# `ARG UBUNTU_BASE_REF` above their FROM and take the value from here.
# `bash ./ctl.sh base-currency` reports a move; the nightly runs it every night.
UBUNTU_BASE_REF=sha256:33ceb71981b602c1a7443a53469e4dba065f7503eab3078a2d7a57a2ab987517   # ubuntu:24.04 index digest as of 2026-08-23

# -------- shell --------
ZSH_VERSION=5.9                                                        # latest LTS as of 2026-04-19

# -------- node toolchain --------
# The nvm digest covers the INSTALLER SCRIPT only: node itself is fetched by
# that script, and node's own download is out of scope. _NOARCH says the 1
# asset serves every platform.
NVM_VERSION=0.40.7                                                     # latest LTS as of 2026-08-24
NVM_SHA256_NOARCH=066ce4eaf4d78eaa6410433bc9ba58faaba646157cbbed6109153e6c24c5f8a5  # computed-at-pin: 2026-08-24
NODE_VERSION=24.19.0                                                   # latest LTS as of 2026-08-17 (Krypton)
NPM_VERSION=12.0.2                                                     # latest LTS as of 2026-08-17
PNPM_VERSION=11.23.0                                                   # what corepack pnpm@latest resolved on 2026-08-24
BUN_VERSION=1.4.0                                                      # latest stable as of 2026-08-24
BUN_SHA256_AMD64=2d03fb5fb83ac8b567aca0a281b2ce1a1a19d488f56c2968d88c3f25e92fe452  # computed-at-pin: 2026-08-24
